# Intent: Encrypted link, the TLS client (off by default, CONFIG_MAIPAI_LINK_PSK). A unit with a stored link key connects to its host only over TLS with the pre-shared key (HKDF of the link key and the device id): the saved ws or http address is rewritten to the host's encrypted listener (ws 8765 to wss 18775, ws 8766 to wss 18776, http 8767 to https 8777) and an address that cannot be rewritten is not connected to. The network component's TLS client uses the key for those ports through esp-tls psk_hint_key; the component is not edited: a configure-time copy adds the lookup (vendor_fixes/link_psk.cmake, only when the switch is on). Also the unit's pairing state machine (maipai_pairx_core.h: pair_start, host key and commitment, nonces, six-digit code, paired) with a host test on the shared vectors; its message handling and screen follow in the next patch.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: managed component 78__esp-ml307 src/esp/esp_ssl.cc (MIT), copied and edited at configure time by firmware/vendor_fixes/link_psk.cmake; firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc (nested tree, MIT); firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: on an image built with the linkpsk overlay and a stored link key the voice socket connects to port 18775 with TLS-PSK; without a stored key behavior is unchanged; on the default image nothing is built.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_LINK_PSK (default n); the linkpsk overlay also sets CONFIG_ESP_TLS_PSK_VERIFICATION

